{"abstract":"This chapter interrogates the question of what defines predictive policing. Our point of departure is notions in Science and Technology Studies that attend to how boundary objects such as predictive policing are produced through the interrelation of politics, sociotechnical imaginaries, and contestations. Through ethnographic inquiry on the empirical case of the POL-INTEL platform of the Danish police, we follow the evolution and demarcations in the (re)-classifications of POL-INTEL from predictive to non-predictive. In so doing, we situate POL-INTEL in the wider international context regarding the development of predictive policing and investigate the boundary work between predictive policing and similar concepts such as Intelligence-Led Policing. Concisely, we argue that the development of the notion of predictive policing is fundamentally unstable and tied to political and economic interests.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Karlsson, Björn","Galis, Vasilis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828160"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Big data","Critical criminology","Digital policing","Law enforcement","Predictive policing","Surveillance technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what constitutes predictive policing the case of pol intel in denmark","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4337/9781035323036","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828160","ids":["itu-7ab4c71c-5a57-4d63-99e4-03f1c7eba8ea"],"keyword":["Big Data","Critical Criminology","Digital Policing","Law Enforcement","Predictive Policing","Surveillance Technology","rime Forecasting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-5-AA0BB3B63F55270DAFE021F87B9FD968"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4337/9781035323036","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4337/9781035323036.00012","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies of Social Order"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Björn","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"3d49de50-0620-46fe-ae15-53b12dfb8649","name":"Karlsson, Björn","orcid":"0009-0006-0393-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","locid":"443362d7-b255-460d-a559-0fa80a8d9fbc","name":"Galis, Vasilis","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-3699","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vasilis","key":"galispedh","last":"Galis","name":"Galis, Vasilis","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Helene O.I.","key":"gundhuspedh","last":"Gundhus","name":"Gundhus, Helene O.I.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Antonis","key":"vradispedh","last":"Vradis","name":"Vradis, Antonis","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4337/9781035323036","eisbn":["9781035323036"],"isbn":["9781035323029"],"pages":"130-155","publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","status":"p","title":"Critical Perspectives on Predictive Policing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004486828","2-s2.0-105004489474"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7ab4c71c-5a57-4d63-99e4-03f1c7eba8ea"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"What constitutes predictive policing? The case of POL-INTEL in Denmark","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828160","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Men develop larger infarct sizes than women after a myocardial infarction (MI), but the mechanism underlying this sex difference is unknown. Here, we demonstrated that blood neutrophil counts post-MI were higher in male than female mice. Castration-induced testosterone deficiency reduced blood neutrophil counts to the level in females and increased survival post-MI. These effects were mimicked by Osterix-directed ablation of the androgen receptor in bone marrow (BM). Mechanistically, androgens downregulated the leukocyte retention factor CXCL12 in BM stromal cells. Post-hoc analysis of clinical trial data showed that neutrophilia was greater in men than women after reperfusion of first-time ST-elevation MI, and tocilizumab, an interleukin-6 receptor inhibitor, reduced blood neutrophil counts and infarct size to a greater extent in men than women. Our work reveals a previously unknown mechanism connecting testosterone with neutrophilia and MI injury via BM and identifies the importance of considering sex when developing anti-inflammatory strategies to treat MI.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Svedlund Eriksson, Elin","Lantero Rodriguez, Marta","Halvorsen, Bente","Johansson, Inger","Mårtensson, Anna K.F.","Wilhelmson, Anna S.","Huse, Camilla","Ueland, Thor","Aukrust, Pål","Broch, Kaspar","Gullestad, Lars","Amundsen, Brage Høyem","Andersen, Geir Øystein","Karlsson, Mikael C.I.","Hagberg Thulin, Malin","Camponeschi, Alessandro","Trompet, Dana","Hammarsten, Ola","Redfors, Björn","Borén, Jan","Omerovic, Elmir","Levin, Malin C.","Chagin, Andrei S.","Dahl, Tuva B.","Tivesten, Åsa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-800229"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Brigham and Women’s Hospital","Karolinska Institutet","Karolinska University Hospital","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Oslo University Hospital","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","St. Olav's University Hospital","University Hospital of North Norway","University of Gothenburg","University of Oslo"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"testosterone exacerbates neutrophilia and cardiac injury in myocardial infarction via actions in bone marrow","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-025-56217-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-800229","identifier":[{"id":"85218189053","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11799197","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39910039","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a7623c46-125d-41c9-9116-994b93b46a39"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-7AB53E56786F8642BF36035B7562A027"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-025-56217-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/431846268/s41467_025_56217_x.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"oslo university hospital","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oslo University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copen