, André","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"19 20","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"billietcharlottepau","last":"Billiet","name":"Billiet, Charlotte","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rolf","key":"lewensohnrolfpau","last":"Lewensohn","name":"Lewensohn, Rolf","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"lindbergkarinpau","last":"Lindberg","name":"Lindberg, Karin","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37423292"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijrobp.2023.06.246","issn":["03603016","1879355X"],"issn_org":["03603016"],"issue":"5","journal":"International Journal of Radiation Oncology, Biology, Physics","pages":"1222-1231","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Radiation Oncology, Biology, Physics","title_org":"International Journal of Radiation Oncology Biology Physics","volume":"117"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85166571260"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1bf76bef-4b5c-4d31-89b2-ac864e83fa12","ku-5a7090c5-712f-4e1f-8e1b-0c0c4744ef27","sdu-3914d343-10f8-48ae-be7d-c52e0cf0e536"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Expanded HILUS Trial : A Pooled Analysis of Risk Factors for Toxicity From Stereotactic Body Radiation Therapy of Central and Ultracentral Lung Tumors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-715884","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: We aimed to describe the uptake of newer biologic or targeted synthetic disease-modifying antirheumatic drugs (b/tsDMARDs) in psoriatic arthritis (PsA) in the Nordic countries and to compare their retention and effectiveness. Methods: Patients with PsA starting a b/tsDMARD in 2012-2020 in five Nordic rheumatology registers were included. Uptake and patient characteristics were described, with comorbidities identified from linkages to national patient registries. One-year retention and 6-month effectiveness (proportions achieving low disease activity (LDA) on the Disease Activity Index for PSoriatic Arthritis based on 28-joint evaluation) for the newer b/tsDMARDs (abatacept/apremilast/ixekizumab/secukinumab/tofacitinib/ustekinumab) were compared with adalimumab through adjusted regression models stratified by treatment course (first, second/third, and fourth or more). Results: In total, 5659 treatment courses with adalimumab (56% biologic-naïve) and 4767 courses with a newer b/tsDMARD (21% biologic-naïve) were included. The uptake of newer b/tsDMARDs increased from 2014 and plateaued in 2018. Patient characteristics appeared similar across treatments at treatment start. Adalimumab was more often used as the first course and newer b/tsDMARDs more often in biologic-experienced patients. Used as a second/third b/tsDMARD, the retention rate and the proportion achieving LDA were significantly better for adalimumab (rate 65%, proportion 59%) compared with abatacept (45%, 37%), apremilast (43%, 35%), ixekizumab (LDA only, 40%) and ustekinumab (LDA only, 40%), but not significantly different from other b/tsDMARDs. Conclusion: Uptake of newer b/tsDMARDs occurred mainly in biologic-experienced patients. Regardless of mode of action, only a minority of patients starting a second or later b/tsDMARD course remained on drug and achieved LDA. Superior outcomes for adalimumab indicate that the positioning of newer b/tsDMARDs in the PsA treatment algorithm remains to be established.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Glintborg, Bente","Di Giuseppe, Daniela","Wallman, Johan Karlsson","Nordström, Dan C","Gudbjornsson, Bjorn","Hetland, Merete Lund","Askling, Johan","Grondal, Gerdur","Sokka, Tuulikki","Provan, Sella A","Michelsen, Brigitte","Kristianslund, Eirik Klami","Dreyer, Lene","Love, Thorvardur Jon","Lindström, Ulf"],"cuid":["S02-099.93-697715"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Glintborg, Bente"],"country":["Finland","Iceland","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Diakonhjemmet Hospital","Helsinki University Hospital","Hospital of Southern Norway","Jyvaskyla Central Hospital","Karolinska Institutet","Karolinska University Hospital","Landspitali University Hospital","Lund University","Skåne University Hospital","University of Eastern Finland","University of Gothenburg","University of Helsinki","University of Iceland"],"keyword":["Biological Therapy","Epidemiology","Spondylitis Ankylosing","Tumor Necrosis Factor Inhibitors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uptake and effectiveness of newer biologic and targeted synthetic disease modifying antirheumatic drugs in psoriatic arthritis results from five nordic biologics registries","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85152661422&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.93-697715","identifier":[{"id":"36813538","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85152661422","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-