"last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"gravennielsenpau","last":"Graven-Nielsen","locid":"474a635b-4e83-4b02-a90b-80d417d37e52","name":"Graven-Nielsen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7787-4860","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Björn","key":"gerdlepau","last":"Gerdle","name":"Gerdle, Björn","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emmanuel","key":"bäckrydpau","last":"Bäckryd","name":"Bäckryd, Emmanuel","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Dag","key":"lemmingpau","last":"Lemming","name":"Lemming, Dag","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35274145"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2340/jrm.v54.241","issn":["16501977","16512081"],"issn_org":["16501977"],"journal":"Journal of Rehabilitation Medicine","paperid":"jrm00286","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Journal of Rehabilitation Medicine","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129781556"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d49ef66f-84d3-47cf-918b-483d1c7b52b4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Pain tolerance in chronic pain patients seems to be more associated with physical activity than with depression and anxiety","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-111814","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Stereotactic body radiation therapy of thoracic tumors close to the central airways implies risk of severe toxicity. We report a prospective multicenter phase 2 trial for tumors located less than or equal to 1 cm from the proximal bronchial tree with primary end point of local control and secondary end point of toxicity. Methods: Stereotactic body radiation therapy with 7 Gy × 8 was prescribed to the 67% isodose encompassing the planning target volume. The patients were stratified to group A (tumors ≤ 1 cm from the main bronchi and trachea) or group B (all other tumors). Risk factors for treatment-related death were tested in univariate analysis, and a logistic regression model was developed for fatal bronchopulmonary bleeding versus dose to the main bronchi and trachea. Results: A total of 65 patients (group A/group B, n = 39/26) were evaluated. The median distance between the tumor and the proximal bronchial tree was 0 mm (0–10 mm). The 2-year local control was 83%. Grade 3 to 5 toxicity was noted in 22 patients, including 10 cases of treatment-related death (bronchopulmonary hemorrhage, n = 8; pneumonitis, n = 1; fistula, n = 1). Dose to the combined structure main bronchi and trachea and tumor distance to the main bronchi were important risk factors. Dose modeling revealed minimum dose to the “hottest” 0.2 cc to the structure main bronchi and trachea as the strongest predictor for lethal bronchopulmonary hemorrhage. Conclusions: On the basis of the presented data, 7 Gy × 8, prescribed to the planning target volume-encompassing isodose, should not be used for tumors located within 1 cm from the main bronchi and trachea. Group B-type tumors may be considered for the treatment on the basis of an individual risk-benefit assessment and a maximum dose to the main bronchi and trachea in the order of 70 to 80 Gy (equivalent dose in 2 Gy fractions).","author_count":27,"contributors":["Lindberg, Karin","Grozman, Vitali","Karlsson, Kristin","Lindberg, Sara","Lax, Ingmar","Wersäll, Peter","Persson, Gitte Fredberg","Josipovic, Mirjana","Khalil, Azza Ahmed","Møller, Ditte Sloth","Nyman, Jan","Drugge, Ninni","Bergström, Per","Olofsson, Jörgen","Rogg, Lotte Victoria","Ramberg, Christina","Kristiansen, Charlotte","Jeppesen, Stefan Starup","Nielsen, Tine Bjørn","Lödén, Britta","Rosenbrand, Hans Olov","Engelholm, Silke","Haraldsson, André","Billiet, Charlotte","Lewensohn, Rolf"],"cuid":["S03-098.99-027741"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Lindberg, Karin"],"country":["Belgium","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Central Hospital Karlstad","Iridium Kankernetwerk","Karlstad Hospital","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Lund University","Oslo University Hospital","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Umeå University","University Hospital of Umeå","University of Antwerp","University of Gothenburg","University of Oslo","e Ystad Hospital , Skåne University Health Care , Region Skåne , Sweden."],"keyword":["Ablative radiotherapy","Cancer","Central","Early stage","Lung tumors","Outcomes","Radiation therapy","Risk","SBRT","Stereotactic","Toxicity","Ultracentral"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the hilus trial a prospective nordic multicenter phase 000000000002 study of ultracentral lung tumors treated with stereotactic body radiotherapy","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type