,"key":"debacquerpau","last":"De Bacquer","name":"De Bacquer, Dirk","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc J","key":"gunterpau","last":"Gunter","name":"Gunter, Marc J","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Inge","key":"huybrechtspau","last":"Huybrechts","name":"Huybrechts, Inge","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34071317"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/nu13061843","issn":["20726643"],"issue":"6","journal":"Nutrients","paperid":"1843","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Nutrients","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106611580"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f477c21c-9c7a-4869-82ff-901056e71e8e","ku-a1c9c541-37ee-4f93-b716-f804739c4e39"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dietary Methyl-Group Donor Intake and Breast Cancer Risk in the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (EPIC)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.50-030310","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Spike-in of standards of known concentrations used in proteomics-based workflows is an attractive approach for both accurate and precise multiplexed protein quantification. Here, a quantitative method based on targeted proteomics analysis of plasma proteins using isotope-labeled recombinant standards originating from the Human Protein Atlas project has been established. The standards were individually quantified prior to being employed in the final multiplex assay. The assays are mainly directed toward actively secreted proteins produced in the liver, but may also originate from other parts of the human body. This study included 21 proteins classified by the FDA as either drug targets or approved clinical protein biomarkers. We describe the use of this multiplex assay for profiling a well-defined human cohort with sample collection spanning over a one-year period. Samples were collected at four different time points, which allowed for a longitudinal analysis to assess the variable plasma proteome within individuals. Two assays toward APOA1 and APOB had available clinical data, and the two assays were benchmarked against each other. The clinical assay is based on antibodies and shows high correlation between the two orthogonal methods, suggesting that targeted proteomics with highly parallel, multiplex analysis is an attractive alternative to antibody-based protein assays.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Kotol, David","Hunt, Helian","Hober, Andreas","Karlsson, Max J.","Forsström, Björn","Gummesson, Anders","Bergström, Göran","Fagerberg, Linn","Uhlén, Mathias","Edfors, Fredrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335000"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Edfors, Fredrik"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Science for Life Laboratory","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Absolute quantification","Blood plasma","Mass spectrometry","Precision medicine","Proteomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"longitudinal plasma protein profiling using targeted proteomics and recombinant protein standards","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85097211012","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-335000","identifier":[{"id":"85097211012","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32820635","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-65f1aec2-4fce-4dde-8abb-8bd9a42ea3e7"],"keyword":["Absolute quantification","Blood plasma","Mass spectrometry","Precision medicine","Proteomics","Recombiant protein standards","Stable isotope standards"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CA5A1E5786CC7BDCCBCC6A1A4C09C86E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"science for life laboratory","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Science for Life Laboratory","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Biosustainability","Technical University of Denmark, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Biosustainability, High Throughput Molecular Bioscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"kotolpau","last":"Kotol","name":"Kotol, David","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helian","key":"huntpau","last":"Hunt","name":"Hunt, Helian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"hoberpau","last":"Hober","name":"Hober, Andreas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Max J.","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","name":"Karlsson, Max J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Björn","key":"forsströmpau","last":"Forsström","name":"Forsström, Björn","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"gummessonpau","last":"Gummesson","name":"Gummesson, Anders","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Göran","key":"bergströmpau","last":"Bergström","name":"Bergström, Göran","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Linn","key":"fagerbergpau","last":"Fagerberg","name":"Fagerberg, Linn","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathias","key":"uhlénpau","last":"Uhlén","locid":"982d3fac-e38d-4933-8ab5-d6eaf128168f","name":"Uhlén, Mathias","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fredrik","key":"edforspau","last":"Edfors","name":"Edfors, Fredrik","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32820635"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jproteome.0c00194","issn":["15353893","15353907"],"issn_org":["15353893"],"issue":"12","journal":"Journal of Proteome Research","pages":"4815-4825","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Proteome Research","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097211012"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-65f1aec2-4fce-4dde-8abb-8bd9a42ea3e7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Longitudinal Plasma Protein Profiling Using Targeted Proteomics and Recombinant Protein Standards","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-335000","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"An important aspect of precision medicine is to probe the stability in molecular profiles among healthy individuals over time. Here, we sample a longitudinal wellness cohort with 100 healthy individuals and analyze blood molecular profiles including proteomics, transcriptomics, lipidomics, metabolomics, autoantibodies and immune cell profiling, complemented with gut microbiota composition and routine clinical chemistry. Overall, our results show high variation between individuals across different molecular readouts, while the intra-individual baseline variation is low. The analyses show that each individual has a unique and stable plasma protein profile throughout the study period and that many individuals also show distinct profiles with regards to the other omics datasets, with strong underlying connections between the blood proteome and the clinical chemistry parameters. In conclusion, the results support an individual-based definition of health and show that comprehensive omics profiling in a longitudinal manner is a path forward for precision medicine.","author_count":38,"contributors":["Tebani, Abdellah","Gummesson, Anders","Zhong, Wen","Koistinen, Ina Schuppe","Lakshmikanth, Tadepally","Olsson, Lisa M.","Boulund, Fredrik","Neiman, Maja","Stenlund, Hans","Hellström, Cecilia","Karlsson, Max J.","Arif, Muhammad","Dodig-Crnković, Tea","Mardinoglu, Adil","Lee, Sunjae","Zhang, Cheng","Chen, Yang","Olin, Axel","Mikes, Jaromir","Danielsson, Hanna","von Feilitzen, Kalle","Jansson, Per-Anders","Angerås, Oskar","Huss, Mikael","Kjellqvist, Sanela","Odeberg, Jacob","Edfors, Fredrik","Tremaroli, Valentina","Forsström, Björn","Schwenk, Jochen M.","Nilsson, Peter","Moritz, Thomas","Bäckhed, Fredrik","Engstrand, Lars","Brodin, Petter","Bergström, Göran","Uhlén, Mathias","Fagerberg, Linn"],"cuid":["S02-099.30-032671"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fagerberg, Linn"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Codon Consulting","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Karolinska Institutet","King's College London","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","Umeå University","University of Gothenburg"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integration of molecular profiles in a longitudinal wellness profiling cohort","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-18148-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.30-032671","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7479148","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32900998","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85090387884","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000607103200020","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-048ea73a-32dd-4b7b-8648-29691c3a85fa","ku-8b812381-0ec7-40a8-a852-3535e600e780"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-71CFD43CD9082514E0BCE86E43106470"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/236340172/s41467_020_18148_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-18148-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/253781341/s41467_020_18148_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"]